posts.body:
Hello,
@hiddenone
first of all, I would like to thank you for being the first person to share your honest and detailed feedback with me. Next, I want to apologize for all the problems you encountered; perhaps if it weren't for those issues, you might have played a bit more and enjoyed other interesting parts I planned for the game. I will respond to the more specific points with a spoiler to avoid disrupting the experience of people who might feel encouraged to try it out. Sorry for the delay in getting back to you! Oh, and your tutorials on the blog were a great help for me to learn more about coding.
Spoiler:
RESPOND-Feedback
Thank you for the compliment about the art. I put a lot of care into this part, choosing palettes and simple designs, and I thought having a more unique look would help me gain points with the audience. The big issue about getting around the place was a system that had been implemented since version 0.1 of the game, but it was removed because it caused problems with other aspects of the game, and I haven't managed to resolve this satisfactorily yet... Currently, Apu's sword hits up to 2 tiles in front of him, but I want to experiment with it hitting the tiles directly in front of Apu as well, but only 1, like an inverted pyramid. Does that make sense? I want to test this to see if it makes the combat experience a bit better.
As for healing, it's something I noticed as more people tested the game. Although they didn't have as many issues as you did, I feel that the game's difficulty has increased a lot with the addition of new areas, but healing has indeed become less effective. Even though I've hidden several hearts in breakable walls and the like, it still doesn't seem to be enough. Improving the chance of hearts dropping from jars and even adding hearts that heal a bit more than 1/4 seem like reasonable suggestions, and I'll look into them carefully.
The bats are indeed tricky enemies, though fragile. I need to see if the adjustment I want to test with the sword makes this more manageable or if they need to be slowed down a bit.
Here are the specific points:
1) I really don't know why I didn't implement this before, haha;
2) This is something I've been facing and don't quite understand why. It also happened with some letters during the player name entry part. Some information images sometimes appear blurry even though I've checked that it's not an issue with the images themselves, and the same images appear in other situations without the blur. Sorry about that;
3) Leave it to me!
4) This was a deliberate choice, but I added hotkeys so the player doesn't have to use items from the backpack as a test. I can check if this has been a problem for players. Somehow, I didn't know how to pause events without it being abused, like entering the menu before a hit and then returning to events;
5) I'll look into this. It probably happens because his sprite is very large;
6) It's like a placeholder. I'm still figuring out a cool system for the stores or a simple design that isn't too much trouble to implement... I'm not sure if you preferred the first one or if walking through the old RPG Maker style is more comfortable;
7) I didn't quite understand this one. Do you mean something like pins on the mini-map indicating the exit?
8) In this case, I think luck was on your side, HAHAHA. They appear randomly on the screen and can come from the middle too. Not having them come from a dangerous direction for you was really lucky. His name is Jintrick, but you can call him Jin;
9) Probably, those were the coins that jumped out of the pots. I must not have configured it well enough to respect the animation time, so the coins walk towards you while the pot destruction animation is still playing.
I hope you give a future version of Apu another chance to see a bit more of the story and the CGs, haha. But even if you prefer to test other games, your feedback was one of the ones that made me happiest. I'll work hard to implement the improvements. Cheers!
